cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Governance, Risk, and Compliance Documentation Library"
abstract: >-
  A CC BY-SA 4.0-licensed reference set for building an
  organization-neutral governance, risk, compliance, security, privacy,
  resilience, supplier, and artificial-intelligence governance
  programme. Includes ~300 documents across 12 domains plus
  jurisdiction-specific privacy annexes and sector-specific compliance
  sub-directories. Also ships the guardrails/ pack, a
  Claude Code rules-and-skills set distilled from the disciplines this
  library required to maintain itself, usable as a standalone Claude
  Code baseline on any project regardless of whether it has a GRC
  corpus.
message: >-
  The CC BY-SA 4.0 licence requires attribution of the library when
  content is redistributed (in original or modified form). Its
  "ShareAlike" condition requires an adopter who shares an adaptation
  to license their own contributions to it under CC BY-SA 4.0, a later
  CC BY-SA version, or a BY-SA-compatible licence. The library's own
  text stays under CC BY-SA 4.0; quoted or vendored third-party
  material keeps its own terms, as NOTICE.md records. This CITATION
  file provides the canonical citation metadata for attribution
  purposes. Adopters using only the guardrails/ pack should still cite
  the parent library, since the pack is a derivative artefact of the
  library's maintenance experience and its GRC-original material ships
  under the same licence.
type: dataset
